WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.440
So I want you to disguise 
me to look human enough

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.820
that I won't scare the other humans.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.410
Surely you can manage that!

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.500
Disguise me to look human!

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:25.140
Before we disguise her, why don't we fix her?

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.420
It stuck!

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.380
<b>Sticks to Anything
Glue</b>

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.380
If you moisten the cracked sections 
with water, it looks a little better.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.720
Huh? The other eye came out, too!

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.980
I'm going to help her change. 
Turn around, you two.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.680
Okay. Your head's stuck on, too.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.770
And the yukata's the perfect size.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:06.120
You still have a few cracks left, but no 
places that look like they're going to break.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:09.130
Do I look human?

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.100
No.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.350
Your face doesn't quite look human.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.180
Your face looks half-transparent to me.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.890
And for those humans 
who can't see yokai...

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.040
Zen... ko?

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:04.330
<b>Mystery 8 "The Removal"</b>

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:03.900
Dad?

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:07.700
She doesn't have a head?

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.210
<i>Keshi-chan's head is invisible to him!</i>

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:26.020
Dad, about the ghost we 
saw at Outlook Ridge...

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:30.140
Is that thing right there a ghost?

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.920
Of course not!

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:32.890
Right!

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.600
A ghost wouldn't come out 
in the middle of the day.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.300
That's right! They wouldn't!

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.800
Then who is she?

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.580
She's... a relative of mine, Keshi-chan!

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.280
She's staying with me over summer vacation.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.080
Right, Abeno-san?

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.610
She said she wanted to attend the 
Outlook Ridge Bon Festival dance,

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.840
so we were having her try 
on one of my old yukata.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.460
Right, Abeno?

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.270
For just one day, I want to become human

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:11.520
and dance with them at 
the Bon Festival dance.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:21.130
Fujiwara-san told me about what's 
going on at Outlook Ridge.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:25.990
Please tell the client there's nothing there.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:30.680
He'll probably feel safer if you tell 
him it was exorcised by a professional.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:35.370
Also, please don't mention our involvement.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.300
I don't mind not telling him, but...

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:43.970
Are you guys going to the 
Bon Festival dance with her?

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.990
Yes. We'll be accompanying her.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:47.690
Yeah.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.810
Dressed like that?

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.160
Let's have some fun before the dance!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.460
Should we scoop goldfish first?

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.730
Hanae, they have shaved ice.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:18.520
Can we, Abeno-san?

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:19.250
Let's expense it.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.710
Thank you!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.970
Keshi-dono, make sure you don't go too wild.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.090
I'll be careful.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.080
Abeno-san, would you like something to eat?

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.150
I'll get something for you.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.890
How do you feel about shaved ice?

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.360
Strawberry? Melon? Lemon?

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.720
Restrain yourself, employee.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.650
Don't forget you're on the clock.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.830
Keshi? What's wrong?

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.830
What should I do?

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:55.320
If I scare them again, I won't 
be able to dance with them.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.510
What if I frighten them?

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:05.320
We'll be looking out for you.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:08.950
Go have a great time, Keshi-chan.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:17.950
Hey, Zenko-chan!

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.320
That must be Keshi-chan.

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.210
Your dad told me about her.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.840
My dad?

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:31.680
Come, come. Let's dance together.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:41.340
<i>The sun is a big, round flower</i>

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:45.400
<i>Our smiles make our faces round</i>

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.360
<i>Ready, and go!</i>

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:57.990
<i>My Sunday lunch is so, so delicious</i>

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:06.490
<i>Mom makes me sandwiches
stuffed full of tasty things</i>

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:10.660
<i>Wa-ha-ha! Kya-kya-kya!</i>

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:14.820
<i>The elephant, the bear, 
and the penguin, too</i>

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.960
<i>No one's afraid of me.</i>

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:19.530
<i>Wa-ha-ha! Kya-kya-kya!</i>

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:19.500
<i>I'm part of the group this time.</i>

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:27.020
<i>Let's all have lots of fun</i>

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.900
<i>I always wanted to be part of the group.</i>

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:31.570
<i>It's a beautiful, sunny day</i>

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:34.040
<i>Ready...</i>

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.450
<i>And now...</i>

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.920
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:45.210
<i>I'm dancing with them.</i>

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.690
Come, come.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.210
Come on.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:56.600
<i>The sun is a big, round flower</i>

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:01.470
<i>My wish finally came true today.</i>

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:00.580
<i>All our friends gather together</i>

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:02.510
<i>Ready, and go!</i>

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:09.280
<i>A Sunday afternoon nap...</i>

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:15.290
Goodbye. Come see us again.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:24.010
That man running the shooting 
game had a nice voice.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:25.780
I thought so, too!

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:28.860
I really envy people with nice voices.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:32.060
Yeah... but I think you have a nice voice, too.

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:33.760
Huh? Me?

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.390
How about here?

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.600
Sure.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:54.760
Master of the Mononokean, Abeno Haruitsuki,

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.530
requesting a portal to the Underworld.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:04.010
Go ahead.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:14.140
Oh, right. I should give 
you your yukata back.

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:15.180
It's okay.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.050
It looks good on you. You can keep it.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.220
You look cute.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:32.460
<i>I had a lot of fun today.</i>

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:36.650
<i>Thank you for granting my wish.</i>

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:43.490
Thank you for making me human, Mononokean.

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:01.880
Zenko, I'll walk you home.

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:02.930
I'm fine.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.400
But...

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:07.100
Don't make her walk home by herself at night.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:11.190
Your dad told me to walk you home.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:15.590
Thanks, then. Why don't you stop 
to rest once we get to my house?

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:16.710
You, too, Abeno.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.100
Nah, I'm good.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:20.000
Okay.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.540
Abeno-san, are you tired?

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:23.640
Not really.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:24.830
Huh?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.640
Abeno-san!

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:31.120
Abeno!

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:33.430
<i>Why?</i>

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:39.260
<i>He only collapses from exhaustion when 
he opens a portal twice in one day.</i>

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.860
<i>But today...</i>

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.930
Oisuke-dono, where is your home?

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.140
My home is under there.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:55.260
It's so hot outside.

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:58.400
Huh?

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.180
Who put this heavy thing here?

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:03.240
My home might be broken!

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.740
I'll move it!

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:08.230
Hey!

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.100
That's our watermelon!

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.020
We're going to break it here!

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:15.600
We claimed this sandbox first, too!

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:16.380
Go away!

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.950
Okay, okay.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:22.510
But first, will you let me 
look for something I lost?

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:24.640
Something you lost?

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.570
How long is that going to take?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.100
Five minutes... No, I'll find it in three!

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:35.020
It'll only take ten seconds to 
break a watermelon, so we're first.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:40.280
You heard them. 
What should we do, Abeno-san?

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.780
<b>Glare</b>

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:44.780
Ten seconds and you'll be done, right?

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:45.780
<i>Blond!</i>

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.160
<i>A cut on his face!</i>

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.160
<i>And a terrifying expression!</i>

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:51.310
<i>O-Oh, no!</i>

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.000
<i>He's a thug in a kimono!</i>

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.680
<i>We picked a fight with a bad man!</i>

00:12:53.000 --> 00:13:01.300
<b>Child Vision On</b>

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.880
If you can't break it in ten seconds...

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.540
Get 'em, bro.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.230
The sun's so bright.

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:06.300
Okay. You guys can have fun first.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:11.350
<b>Child Vision On</b>

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.890
We'll take our time looking for it after.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.960
Even if they let us stay, they won't spare us!

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.730
We'll have to break it in ten seconds.

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:20.560
Let's go!

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:23.610
I'll count you down. Ten, nine...

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:28.110
They're going to hit it with that stick?! 
They'll break my home doing that!

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:29.570
When did he get there?

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.460
Stop!

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:48.440
Wow...

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:51.270
That was a real-life flying kick...

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:54.470
Thugs are awesome!

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:59.350
<b>Child Vision On</b>

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:00.820
Thugs?

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:12.010
My sweet home!

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:15.370
I'm going to exorcise Oisuke-dono over there.

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:19.580
Make sure the kids don't follow me.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.200
Got it.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:22.740
Hairball, come with me.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:31.520
<i>If this job had come from the Executive,</i>

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:34.680
<i>Abeno-san would've come alone.</i>

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:38.200
<i>In that moment, if I hadn't stopped him...</i>

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:42.440
<i>Once again, he would've 
done something reckless.</i>

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:02.620
Master of the Mononokean, Abeno Haruitsuki,

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:04.820
requesting a portal to the Underworld.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:18.720
Oisuke-dono, is there any damage?

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:21.730
No problem. My home is undamaged.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:25.230
I have Ashiya-dono to thank for 
risking himself to protect it.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:29.030
He saved it with that kick as 
it was about to be split apart.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:33.980
<i>But it wasn't necessary to 
use acrobatics to save it.</i>

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:36.110
<i>One misstep,</i>

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:36.700
<b>POW</b>

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:40.170
<i>and we might've been digging 
a grave in that sandbox.</i>

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.240
<b>WHUD</b>

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:42.250
<b>SPLAT</b>

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:41.620
Abeno-dono.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:42.250
<b>My home</b>

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:47.300
Tell Ashiya-dono that I'm grateful.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:50.050
Very well.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:04.020
It's my turn next.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.660
Left, left!

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:07.690
Which way is left?

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.580
Oisuke-dono said he was grateful.

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:13.820
He said he had you to thank 
for risking yourself.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:16.700
Really?

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:19.700
I'm glad I could protect his home.

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:22.580
But you didn't need to jump like that.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.650
But if I hadn't stopped you,

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:27.230
you would've risked yourself 
to protect it, right?

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:28.470
Jumped right in.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.990
That never even crossed my mind.

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:38.600
Liar. The thought was 
definitely in your head.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:45.530
I thought you were about to get 
injured in front of me again.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:49.020
That scratch on your cheek...

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:52.220
You got it when you tried 
to tackle a job alone

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:55.660
to keep me away from the Executive,

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:59.990
and then collapsed because you hid 
it from me out of consideration.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:04.940
But next time,

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:10.070
if you get a job from the Executive, 
I want you to let me know.

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:14.050
If you do something reckless again,

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:17.290
I'll at least ensure that 
you have a lifeline.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:25.940
Also, you may not know 
this, but I'm actually...

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.940
an employee of the Mononokean.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:33.280
<b>Dumbfounded</b>

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:33.280
Huh?

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:37.070
I may be a greenhorn,
but I'll help with any job.

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.780
Don't be afraid to ask for help.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.540
Really?

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:48.300
You're an employee of the Mononokean?

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:52.380
I had no idea.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:53.860
I know, right?

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:57.760
You have an employee called Fuzzy, too.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:00.010
I know that.

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:04.270
Abeno-san, you're next!

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:06.140
Abeno-san, over here!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.160
Come on, Abeno-san!

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:09.520
You can do it without a handicap!

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:14.670
Imagine the watermelon is 
an enemy thug and hit it.

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:16.200
Have you ever swung a metal pipe around

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.730
while riding a motorcycle 
and broken a window?

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:21.030
Abeno-san!

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:24.700
I'll guide you to the watermelon!

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.230
Itsuki.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:42.440
I'll probably have another job 
for the Mononokean in the future.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:44.310
When I do,

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:49.690
don't hesitate to use Ashiya Hanae.

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:55.720
That's only if that human hasn't fled in fear

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:59.800
and is still your employee, that is.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:04.590
There! Watch out for the step!

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:06.060
Yeah, go!

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:06.830
Careful!

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:07.880
Don't kill anyone!

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:09.080
Go for it!

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:11.880
Keep going straight!

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.210
It's right there! Go!

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:23.220
<i>Executive, your plan failed.</i>

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.220
Impressive!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:26.620
That's a thug for you!

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:27.810
In just one hit!

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:37.770
What a great watermelon!

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:49.830
You were late because you 
were splitting a watermelon.

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:52.420
Yeah. We said no at first, 
but the kids insisted.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:55.750
We thought it'd be easier 
than having them follow us.

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:01.930
Mononokean, about our plans 
for the rest of the week...

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:03.530
Your school uniform?

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:05.950
Do you have another job after this?

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:08.470
That was the only job we had today.

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:10.680
Really?

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:14.690
We really are closed for the day.

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:17.870
If the Mononokean says so, 
then it must be true.

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:18.840
Ashiya.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:19.720
Yes?

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:23.700
We don't have any jobs from 
the Executive right now.

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:25.780
Right?

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:31.000
We currently have zero 
jobs from the Executive.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:37.960
If he hires us again, this time...

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:42.010
I could use your help.

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:44.620
<i>He doesn't seem to want to ask.</i>

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:49.340
<i>Even so, next time he'll tell 
me instead of hiding it.</i>

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:57.020
Don't be afraid to ask for help.

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.080
It's lukewarm.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:08.680
I tried to cool it in water.

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:12.410
Mononokean, class is resuming next week.

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.440
I want to organize our schedule.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.630
<i>Summer vacation is almost over.</i>

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:21.800
<i>It was a long summer.</i>

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.020
It's good.

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time: "The Shadow"</b>

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:27.790
My mom collapses and 
ends up in the hospital!

00:23:27.790 --> 00:23:30.430
The shadow of a yokai flickers 
in and out of sight...

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:32.150
And my sister comes home!

00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:34.140
Next time, "The Shadow."

00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:38.560
The Ashiya family's secrets are 
finally revealed... maybe?
